    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d427">

                <pb facs="0421" n="411" sameAs="frus:frus1941v06/pg411"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">824.796/207: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Bolivia</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Dawson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-12-09T01:00:00-05:00">December 9, 1941—1
                        a.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>252. Your 346, November 29, and despatch 1167, October 8.<anchor n="31"
                        xml:id="d427-f1"/> Department, Panagra and the Defense Supplies Corporation
                    have no <pb facs="0422" n="412" xml:id="pg412"/> objection to the transfer of
                    control of civil and commercial aviation from the Ministry of Communications to
                    the Ministry of Defense, provided it is clearly understood with the Foreign
                    Office that the obligation entered into by the Ministry of Communications with
                    the Defense Supplies Corporation will be assumed by the Ministry of Defense.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d427-f1" n="31" xml:id="d427-f1-content">
                <p>Latter not printed.</p>
